      "message": "feat(post): pause or home after an operation; suppress ops; skip pauses and homes\n\nEach operation now carries an after-action (Operation.after, the post\ncrate's AfterOperation): Continue (default), Optional stop, Program stop\nor Go home. Continue is the stream's silent default, so every CL/NC\ngolden stays byte-exact.\n\n- Stream: any other choice rides one PARAM AfterOperation\n  optional-stop|stop|home ahead of the section (the #112 coolant\n  pattern).\n- Posts: afterOp() writes the dialect's words after the section's\n  spindle stop. Fanuc/Haas/Mazak M1 / M0, home G91 G28 Z0, G28 X0 Y0,\n  G90. Siemens 840D M1 / M0, home G0 G53 Z0 then G0 G53 X0 Y0. Fanuc\n  Lathe M01 / M00, home G28 U0 then G28 W0. Heidenhain M1 / M0; a\n  Heidenhain home is a counted message() naming the post (#50: no\n  machine-referenced home it can trust), so the gate blocks it.\n- Suppress: Operation.suppressed. posting::program_ops drops suppressed\n  ops before the freshness law, so the post, the program sim and the\n  limit check all skip them. The toolpath and stamp are kept. If every\n  op is suppressed, the post refuses by name.\n- Skip pauses and homes: a PostOptions singleton switched by the\n  undoable SetPostOptions command (a checkbox under the Post picker).\n  It mutes every after-action at post; the ops keep their choices.\n- Commands: EditOperationParams::with_after / with_suppressed, one\n  undo unit each.\n- UI: the op context menu gets \"Suppress operation\" / \"Unsuppress\n  operation\" and an \"After: ...\" row that steps through the choices.\n  The tree row shows SUPPRESSED / \"then <action>\".\n- Project file: \"after\", \"suppressed\" and the top-level \"skip_stops\"\n  are written only off their defaults; older files load with the\n  defaults, no version bump.\n\nStandalone Pause / Home list entries are owed: #155.\n\nFixes #110\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
