      },
      "message": "fix(post): refuse a post that drops a suppressed cut a later op assumed; afterModes manifest flag\n\nReview B1: rest machining and the generation-time rapid verdicts walk\nthe setup's operation order with no suppressed filter, so a later op\nis generated against a suppressed op's cut. verification_report now\nrefuses by name when a posted op that reads the program ahead\n(operation::reads_prior) has a suppressed, cutting op ahead of it in\nits setup (rest::suppressed_cuts_ahead): \"operation Rest2 was\ngenerated against the cut of suppressed Rough1; unsuppress Rough1 or\nsuppress Rest2 too\". The per-op post runs the same gate.\n\nReview B2: the engine refuses any PARAM AfterOperation, by operation\nname, for a script that does not declare afterModes = true (the\ncoolantModes pattern of #150); the six shipped posts that write\nafterOp() declare it.\n\nReview notes: Fanuc drops TCPM (G49) before a Go-home reference\nreturn; the Heidenhain home refusal and every unknown-ask refusal name\nthe operation. The engine's coolantModes refusal text loses a run of\nstray spaces.\n\nPinned by suppressed_rest (both tests) and\npost_engine::a_stop_asked_of_a_script_without_after_modes_is_refused_by_name.\n\nRefs #110\nRefs #111\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
